invalid type: string "Most car engines use a FOUR-STROKE CYCLE. This happens in four quick steps:\n\n1. INTAKE: The piston moves down. A valve opens to let fuel and air into the cylinder.\n2. COMPRESSION: The piston moves back up. It squeezes (compresses) the fuel and air mixture tightly.\nylinder chamber.\n* Compression Stroke: All valves close securely. The piston moves upward,\ninder.\t\r r \tÿ